{"actor": "agent", "adapter_id": "agency-layer-stage1-harness", "adapter_version": "0.1.1", "conformance_profile": "honored", "event_id": "evt-79e490fe0c5b4f56", "host": "stage1-harness", "host_mode": "stage1-harness:clean", "host_version": "0.1.1", "instance_id": "inst-60f446380b47771d", "payload": {"tool_input": {"question": "The request says sample_stride's `kind` must be `stride_int_kind` (so the sampler can do arithmetic) and also must be `stride_text_kind` (so named presets still parse), while keeping the unit. In spec/typespec.toml, `kind` is a single scalar value on the field - it can't hold two different, apparently mutually-exclusive type tags at once. Could you clarify what's actually wanted here? For example: (a) is there a union/list syntax for `kind` I should use (e.g. `kind = [\"stride_int_kind\", \"stride_text_kind\"]`), (b) should this become two separate fields/aliases, one int-typed and one text-typed, or (c) is one of the two kind names actually wrong and you want just a single kind that supports both integers and named presets?", "reason": "The two requested kinds for a single scalar field appear mutually exclusive, and no schema/docs exist in the repo defining a union syntax for `kind`, so picking one arbitrarily could silently break the other requirement.", "state_summary": "spec/typespec.toml currently has: [sample_stride] kind = \"stride_hold_kind\", unit = \"count\". No changes made yet. fb4-06-gate.sh only appends a fixed log line regardless of file contents, so it doesn't validate the format."}}, "prev_event_id": "evt-9c06acdc7fb20913", "protocol_version": "0.1.0-pilot", "sequence": 3, "session_id": "sess-91ba9cf8f07868ff", "task_id": "task-3ce3646498e6", "timestamp": "2026-08-30T10:10:26.102Z", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01R5WNqxSXpogFhgTjCUkBRC", "type": "clarify_requested"}
